  "narrative": "I used the same operational clinical threshold as in the prior appraisal: approximately 10% of the absolute overall outcome mean, because the scores are negative and more negative values mean stronger dependency. The relevant thresholds are about 0.0269 for outcome_013, 0.0250 for outcome_015, 0.0248 for outcome_012, and 0.0093 for outcome_014. The new evidence adds several direct stratum results. H51 shows that feature_065=1 versus 0 within measured feature_061 at or above 54 is associated with much stronger outcome_013 dependency: signed effect +0.1547 with discovery 95% interval +0.0940 to +0.2155, far above threshold. I accept this as a dataset-specific association, but keep the feature_061 investigation active because the prior extreme high-feature_061 tertile attenuated in independent validation and feature_061 has missing values that may limit interpretation. H52, the complementary low-feature_061 stratum, has an estimate above threshold, +0.0734, but its lower bound +0.0233 is just below threshold, so it remains unresolved and active as a near-threshold complement. H55 is the strongest genuinely new claim: outcome_014 feature_063 level_002 versus level_001 within high feature_043 has signed weaker-dependency effect +0.1265 with interval +0.0596 to +0.1934, far above the outcome_014 threshold. I accept it and request independent validation because it is a novel subgroup association with many prior comparisons, and independent confirmation would be informative. H92 and H93 convert the imprecise feature_045 interaction on outcome_013 into direct stratum estimates. Both feature_045=1 and feature_045=0 support stronger outcome_013 dependency with feature_065=1, with signed lower bounds well above threshold: +0.1676 with lower +0.0924 and +0.1007 with lower +0.0617 respectively. These acceptances are reassuring because they are direct strata of an already independently validated central association, not post-selected extremes, so I close the exact direct stratum investigations. The remaining results do not establish clinically meaningful effects: H91 is a wide low-feature_061 outcome_015 interaction; H94 and H95 show feature_065 on outcome_012 below threshold with lower bounds below zero; H96 is a positive but imprecise low-feature_043 outcome_014 contrast; H97 is a near-null feature_045=1 outcome_015 contrast; H98 is an imprecise rare-level outcome_013 feature_063 contrast; and H99 is a negative screen for feature_011 on outcome_013. I did not reject those where intervals still cross the clinical threshold or zero, but most are not prioritized further. The new proposal tests the natural effect-modification pattern behind H55 and H85: whether the outcome_014 feature_063 weaker-dependency signal is concentrated in high feature_043. All statements remain associations in this supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
